{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6e55501a-e60c-4288-a21e-18c74c4c887f",
    "name": "EZ Key Enrollments auth",
    "description": "Collection for mobile device enrollment operations in the Auth API.\n\n## Error format (4xx/5xx)\n\nHTTP errors use RFC 9457 Problem Details (`application/problem+json`). See `docs/ENDPOINT.md`.\n\n## Cryptographic protocol\n\nEnrollment uses **canonical pipe-separated UTF-8 payloads** (see `docs/ENROLLMENT_SIGNATURE_PAYLOAD.md` and `docs/MOBILE_DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md`):\n\n- **Bind response:** verify integration Ed25519 signature on the bind payload before trusting metadata.\n- **Verify request:** device ECDSA signature covers `enrollmentProofToken|enrollmentId|challengeResponse|devicePublicKey` — **not** the raw proof token alone.\n- **Verify response:** verify integration Ed25519 signature on the verify-result payload before treating enrollment as complete.\n\nThis collection mirrors **EZ Key Auth Attempts auth** (payload-helper → verify-ed25519 → device sign → Auth API → payload-helper → verify-ed25519).\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nSet `enrollmentId`, `enrollmentProofToken`, and `enrollmentChallenge` in the environment (from Admin enrollment creation) **before** step 1. The Crypto API (`base_url_crypto_api`) must be reachable.\n\n## Flow (numbered requests)\n\n1. Bind — Auth API\n2. Crypto build enrollment bind payload — `payload-helper` `enrollment-bind`\n3. Crypto validate bind signature — Ed25519 verify\n4. Crypto generate device keypair\n5. Crypto build enrollment verify device payload — `payload-helper` `enrollment-verify-device`\n6. Crypto sign verify device payload — ECDSA over canonical string from step 5\n7. Verify — Auth API\n8. Crypto build enrollment verify result payload — `payload-helper` `enrollment-verify-result`\n9. Crypto validate verify result signature — Ed25519 verify\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "4087"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 bind",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200, 400, or 409\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([200, 400, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentId\", jsonData.enrollmentId);",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"integrationPublicKey\", jsonData.integrationPublicKey);",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"integrationKeyAlgorithm\", jsonData.integrationKeyAlgorithm);",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentProofToken\", jsonData.enrollmentProofToken);",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentBindPayloadSignedByIntegration\", jsonData.enrollmentBindPayloadSignedByIntegration);",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"bind_integrationName\", jsonData.integrationName != null ? jsonData.integrationName : \"\");",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"bind_integrationDescription\", jsonData.integrationDescription != null ? jsonData.integrationDescription : \"\");",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"bind_enrollmentName\", jsonData.enrollmentName != null ? jsonData.enrollmentName : \"\");",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"bind_tenantId\", jsonData.tenantId != null ? String(jsonData.tenantId) : \"\");",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"bind_tenantName\", jsonData.tenantName != null ? jsonData.tenantName : \"\");",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"bind_tenantDescription\", jsonData.tenantDescription != null ? jsonData.tenantDescription : \"\");",
              "    pm.test(\"Response contains required fields\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('enrollmentId');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('integrationPublicKey');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('integrationKeyAlgorithm');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('enrollmentProofToken');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('enrollmentBindPayloadSignedByIntegration');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\r\n    \"enrollmentId\": {{enrollmentId}},\r\n    \"enrollmentProofToken\": \"{{enrollmentProofToken}}\"\r\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/enrollments/bind",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "enrollments",
            "bind"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Initiates device binding. On **200**, persist integration metadata and `enrollmentBindPayloadSignedByIntegration` for the next steps.\n\n**Next:** Run **2** to build the canonical bind payload, then **3** to verify the integration Ed25519 signature.\n\nSee `docs/MOBILE_DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md` (bind response)."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "2 crypto build enrollment bind payload",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var tid = pm.environment.get(\"bind_tenantId\");",
              "var body = {",
              "    type: \"enrollment-bind\",",
              "    proofToken: pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentProofToken\"),",
              "    enrollmentId: Number(pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentId\")),",
              "    integrationPublicKey: pm.environment.get(\"integrationPublicKey\"),",
              "    integrationKeyAlgorithm: pm.environment.get(\"integrationKeyAlgorithm\"),",
              "    integrationName: pm.environment.get(\"bind_integrationName\") || null,",
              "    integrationDescription: pm.environment.get(\"bind_integrationDescription\") || null,",
              "    enrollmentName: pm.environment.get(\"bind_enrollmentName\") || null,",
              "    tenantId: tid === \"\" || tid === undefined ? null : Number(tid),",
              "    tenantName: pm.environment.get(\"bind_tenantName\") || null,",
              "    tenantDescription: pm.environment.get(\"bind_tenantDescription\") || null",
              "};",
              "pm.request.body.raw = JSON.stringify(body);"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentBindPayload\", jsonData.payload);",
              "    pm.test(\"Payload helper returned enrollment-bind payload\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.type).to.equal('enrollment-bind');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.payload).to.be.a('string');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_crypto_api}}/api/v1/crypto/payload-helper",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_crypto_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "crypto",
            "payload-helper"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Builds the canonical bind payload via Crypto API (same rules as `EnrollmentSignaturePayload` in `ezkey-core`). Run immediately after **1 bind** (200).\n\n**Next:** **3** — verify `enrollmentBindPayloadSignedByIntegration` with `verify-ed25519`."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3 crypto validate enrollment bind by integration",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var payload = pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentBindPayload\");",
              "if (!payload) {",
              "    throw new Error(\"Run step 2 first — enrollmentBindPayload is missing.\");",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.test(\"Bind payload signature is valid\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.valid).to.be.true;",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\r\n    \"data\": \"{{enrollmentBindPayload}}\",\r\n    \"signature\": \"{{enrollmentBindPayloadSignedByIntegration}}\",\r\n    \"publicKey\": \"{{integrationPublicKey}}\"\r\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_crypto_api}}/api/v1/crypto/verify-ed25519",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_crypto_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "crypto",
            "verify-ed25519"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Verifies the integration Ed25519 signature on the bind payload before trusting enrollment metadata (see `docs/ENROLLMENT_SIGNATURE_PAYLOAD.md`)."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "4 crypto generate device keypair",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"device_privateKey\", jsonData.privateKey);",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"device_publicKey\", jsonData.publicKey);",
              "    pm.test(\"Response contains required fields\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('privateKey');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('publicKey');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_crypto_api}}/api/v1/crypto/keypair",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_crypto_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "crypto",
            "keypair"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Generates an EC P-256 key pair for the simulated device (production: on-device keystore)."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "5 crypto build enrollment verify device payload",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var ch = pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentChallenge\");",
              "if (ch === undefined || ch === null || ch === \"\") {",
              "    throw new Error(\"Set enrollmentChallenge in the environment (from Admin enrollment creation).\");",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentVerifyDevicePayload\", jsonData.payload);",
              "    pm.test(\"Payload helper returned enrollment-verify-device payload\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.type).to.equal('enrollment-verify-device');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.payload).to.be.a('string');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\r\n    \"type\": \"enrollment-verify-device\",\r\n    \"proofToken\": \"{{enrollmentProofToken}}\",\r\n    \"enrollmentId\": {{enrollmentId}},\r\n    \"challengeResponse\": {{enrollmentChallenge}},\r\n    \"devicePublicKey\": \"{{device_publicKey}}\"\r\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_crypto_api}}/api/v1/crypto/payload-helper",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_crypto_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "crypto",
            "payload-helper"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Builds the canonical string that the device must sign for verify: `enrollmentProofToken|enrollmentId|challengeResponse|devicePublicKey` (see `docs/ENROLLMENT_SIGNATURE_PAYLOAD.md`).\n\n**Prerequisite:** `enrollmentChallenge` in the environment."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "6 crypto sign enrollment verify device payload",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var p = pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentVerifyDevicePayload\");",
              "if (!p) {",
              "    throw new Error(\"Run step 5 first — enrollmentVerifyDevicePayload is missing.\");",
              "}",
              "var pk = pm.environment.get(\"device_privateKey\");",
              "pm.request.body.raw = JSON.stringify({ data: p, privateKey: pk });"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentProofTokenSigned\", jsonData.signature);",
              "    pm.test(\"Response contains signature\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('signature');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_crypto_api}}/api/v1/crypto/sign",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_crypto_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "crypto",
            "sign"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Signs the **canonical verify-device payload** from step 5 with the device private key. The result is `enrollmentProofTokenSigned` for **7 verify** — do **not** sign the raw proof token alone."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "7 verify",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200, 400, or 409\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([200, 400, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentVerifyMessage\", jsonData.enrollmentVerifyMessage != null ? jsonData.enrollmentVerifyMessage : \"\");",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentVerifyPayloadSignedByIntegration\", jsonData.enrollmentVerifyPayloadSignedByIntegration);",
              "    pm.test(\"Response contains active field\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('active');",
              "    });",
              "    pm.test(\"Enrollment is active\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.active).to.be.true;",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\r\n    \"enrollmentId\": {{enrollmentId}},\r\n    \"challengeResponse\": {{enrollmentChallenge}},\r\n    \"devicePublicKey\": \"{{device_publicKey}}\",\r\n    \"enrollmentProofTokenSigned\": \"{{enrollmentProofTokenSigned}}\",\r\n    \"devicePrivateKeyStorageTier\": \"STANDARD\"\r\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/enrollments/verify",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "enrollments",
            "verify"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Completes enrollment verification. `enrollmentProofTokenSigned` must be ECDSA over the canonical verify-device string from step 5–6.\n\n**Next:** **8** and **9** validate the integration signature on the verify HTTP response."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "8 crypto build enrollment verify result payload",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var msg = pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentVerifyMessage\");",
              "if (msg === undefined) {",
              "    throw new Error(\"Run step 7 verify (200) first — enrollmentVerifyMessage is missing.\");",
              "}",
              "var body = {",
              "    type: \"enrollment-verify-result\",",
              "    proofToken: pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentProofToken\"),",
              "    enrollmentId: Number(pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentId\")),",
              "    result: \"VERIFIED\",",
              "    message: msg",
              "};",
              "pm.request.body.raw = JSON.stringify(body);"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"enrollmentVerifyResultPayload\", jsonData.payload);",
              "    pm.test(\"Payload helper returned enrollment-verify-result payload\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.type).to.equal('enrollment-verify-result');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.payload).to.be.a('string');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_crypto_api}}/api/v1/crypto/payload-helper",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_crypto_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "crypto",
            "payload-helper"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Builds the canonical verify-result payload for Ed25519 verification (same as server). Run after **7 verify** (200)."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "9 crypto validate enrollment verify result by integration",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "var payload = pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentVerifyResultPayload\");",
              "if (!payload) {",
              "    throw new Error(\"Run step 8 first — enrollmentVerifyResultPayload is missing.\");",
              "}",
              "var sig = pm.environment.get(\"enrollmentVerifyPayloadSignedByIntegration\");",
              "if (!sig) {",
              "    throw new Error(\"Run step 7 verify (200) first — enrollmentVerifyPayloadSignedByIntegration is missing.\");",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.test(\"Verify-result signature cryptographically valid\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.valid).to.be.true;",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\r\n    \"data\": \"{{enrollmentVerifyResultPayload}}\",\r\n    \"signature\": \"{{enrollmentVerifyPayloadSignedByIntegration}}\",\r\n    \"publicKey\": \"{{integrationPublicKey}}\"\r\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_crypto_api}}/api/v1/crypto/verify-ed25519",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_crypto_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "crypto",
            "verify-ed25519"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Verifies the integration Ed25519 signature on the verify HTTP response (`enrollmentVerifyPayloadSignedByIntegration`). End-to-end assurance in Postman."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ],
